<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Monster</h1>
<p>A monster, also called a mobile, a mob or an NPC (a non-player character), 
is any character the game itself controls: the dragon in its lair, but 
also the shopkeeper, the guard at the gate, the guild master and the 
rabbit in the field.
</p><p>Some monsters will attack you on sight; most leave you alone until you 
attack them. Before you pick a fight, <a cmd='#'>consider</a> your foe, and remember 
that some monsters call for help or flee. Killing monsters is how you 
earn most of your experience (see <a cmd='#'>Help Experience</a>); what they carry is 
left in their corpse.
</p><p>Townsfolk such as shopkeepers and guards are often protected by the law: 
killing one is a crime (see <a cmd='#'>Help Laws</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
